SUMMARY:Folk & Blues with Tal Naccarato
DESCRIPTION:About the program\n\nTal Naccarato performs solo acoustic music 
 from his original and traditional repertoire as a singer-songwriter and 
 guitarist in the Americana\, folk\, and blues genres. Rare vintage 
 instruments are demonstrated during the performance\, along with talks 
 about the various musical genres. \n\n \n\nAbout the artist\n\nTal 
 Naccarato is a vibrant composer\, songwriter\, and teaching artist whose 
 roots stretch from the medieval mountain village of Fiumefreddo\, Bruzio\, 
 Italy\, to the vibrant community of East Flatbush\, Brooklyn. His original 
 music is a mix of folk\, Americana\, rock\, and blues\, mixed with 
 classical guitar elements and a distinct bluesy swing. Tal was the 
 first-place winner in the Long Island Blues Society Solo/Duo Competition in 
 2023. He performs solo acoustic shows\, both with original music and 
 traditional songs.
LOCATION:West Orange - Community Room 1
ORGANIZER;CN="West Orange Library":MAILTO:events@westorange.bccls.org
CATEGORIES:Performance
UID:LibCal-10341-17690175
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17690175
